From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: georgewhewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 05:48:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: ignore XDomain peers with the local UUID

Hub-mediated host-to-host experiments can expose a routed XDomain entry whose
UUID is the local host UUID. Upstream treats that as a loop and continues the
handshake with lane bonding disabled, which makes the loop visible as a Linux
host and lets services bind to a stale self route.

For these bridge tests, do not enumerate self-UUID XDomains. Stop discovery
after the UUID exchange so only real remote domains can reach properties and
service binding.
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c
@@ -1218,12 +1218,16 @@ static int tb_xdomain_get_uuid(struct tb
 	dev_dbg(&xd->dev, "got remote UUID %pUb\n", &uuid);
 
 	if (uuid_equal(&uuid, xd->local_uuid)) {
-		if (route == xd->route)
+		if (route == xd->route)
 			dev_dbg(&xd->dev, "loop back detected\n");
 		else
 			dev_dbg(&xd->dev, "intra-domain loop detected\n");
 
 		/* Don't bond lanes automatically for loops */
 		xd->bonding_possible = false;
+		dev_info(&xd->dev,
+			 "ignoring XDomain peer with local UUID %pUb route=%llx remote_route=%llx\n",
+			 &uuid, xd->route, route);
+		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
 	/*
